Relevant columns, their potential usage and basic conditions  
`311_service_requests.complaint_type` : categorical variable whose relationship with temperature must be analysed (filter ≥ 5 000 total rows)  
`311_service_requests.created_date` : exact date‑time stamp; will be truncated to the calendar‑day that matches the GSOD weather records  
`311_service_requests.unique_key` : allows fast counting / de‑duplication if necessary  

`gsodYYYY.stn` : choose only “725030”  (LaGuardia) and “744860” (JFK)  
`gsodYYYY.year`, `gsodYYYY.mo`, `gsodYYYY.da` : compose the full calendar date that will be joined to 311 dates  
`gsodYYYY.temp` : daily mean air temperature ( °F × 0.1 ); use only rows where `temp < 9999.9`  
`gsodYYYY.flag_max` / `flag_min` … : **not used** here  

Basic date and quality conditions that will repeatedly appear  
• `stn IN ('725030','744860')`  
• `temp < 9999.9`                          -- remove “missing” flag value  
• `PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', CONCAT(year, LPAD(mo,2,'0'), LPAD(da,2,'0'))) BETWEEN '2008-01-01' AND '2017-12-31'`  

